WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:07.920
Okay, so with that, we have enough fundamentals in order to start talking about the views.

00:07.920 --> 00:10.280
So the question is what are views?

00:10.320 --> 00:17.800
A view is a virtual table in SQL that is based on the result of a query without actually storing the

00:17.800 --> 00:19.200
data in the database.

00:19.360 --> 00:24.000
So in short, this means views are stored or persisted.

00:24.360 --> 00:26.280
SQL query in the database.

00:26.400 --> 00:28.520
So let's understand what this exactly means.

00:28.560 --> 00:32.360
Now so far what you have learned we have like a database table and all what you have done.

00:32.360 --> 00:36.600
We create a Select query in order to retrieve the data from this table.

00:36.600 --> 00:39.640
So once we execute our query, we will get the result back.

00:39.640 --> 00:45.560
Now if we are talking about views they have as well like the structure of the table but without any

00:45.560 --> 00:46.560
data inside it.

00:46.560 --> 00:50.520
And for each view there is like a query attached to it.

00:50.520 --> 00:53.280
So there is no data, but we have like a query.

00:53.320 --> 00:59.080
In order to get data, we call the normal table as a physical table and the view we call it a virtual

00:59.120 --> 00:59.680
table.

00:59.680 --> 01:01.920
So now how exactly we are going to get the data.

01:01.920 --> 01:07.720
So now if you go and write query by selecting data from the view not from the table from the view,

01:07.760 --> 01:08.800
what can happen?

01:08.840 --> 01:13.240
Is SQL going to go and trigger the queue that is attached to the view.

01:13.280 --> 01:17.560
And this query is responsible to query the physical table.

01:17.560 --> 01:20.440
And then the result is going to fill the structure of the view.

01:20.440 --> 01:22.640
And we will get back of course the results.

01:22.640 --> 01:24.920
So we are directly querying a view.

01:24.920 --> 01:28.880
But actually we are indirectly querying a physical table.

01:28.880 --> 01:31.640
So the view is like between us and the data.

01:31.640 --> 01:35.400
So that means my real data is stored inside the database tables.

01:35.400 --> 01:40.360
And the views are like an abstraction layer between me and my real data.

01:40.360 --> 01:43.440
And of course the data will not be stored inside the view.

01:43.720 --> 01:46.920
Each time I'm querying the view, what's going to happen?

01:46.960 --> 01:50.160
The SQL query behind the view is going to be executed again.

01:50.160 --> 01:53.000
So it's going to go and retrieve the data and get it back to the view.

01:53.000 --> 01:54.720
And then I will see it in the output.

01:54.720 --> 01:57.520
So this is what we mean with SQL view.
